---
number: 629
title: Jesus Calls the Children Dear
author: C. H. Woolston
composer: George F. Root
sp_category: "40"
topic: Children
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
Jesus calls the children dear,
“Come to Me and never fear,
For I love the little children of the world;
I will take you by the hand,
Lead you to the better land,
For I love the little children of the world.”

[chorus]
Jesus loves the little children,
All the children of the world;
Red and yellow, black and white,
They are precious in His sight,
Jesus loves the little children of the world.

[verse 2]
Jesus is the Shepherd true,
And He’ll always stand by you,
For He loves the little children of the world;
He’s a Saviour great and strong,
And He’ll shield you from the wrong,
For He loves the little children of the world.

[chorus]
Jesus loves the little children,
All the children of the world;
Red and yellow, black and white,
They are precious in His sight,
Jesus loves the little children of the world.

[verse 3]
I am coming, Lord, to Thee,
And Thy soldier I will be,
For He loves the little children of the world;
And His cross I’ll always bear,
And for Him I’ll do and dare,
For He loves the little children of the world.

[chorus]
Jesus loves the little children,
All the children of the world;
Red and yellow, black and white,
They are precious in His sight,
Jesus loves the little children of the world.
